# ZP-20261101-11 application-side controls. This file contains no credentials.
# Inject into BOTH API and worker containers (Compose backend/.env or K8s env).
# Default denies user-configured source connections until approved exact
# numeric IP:port destinations are reviewed and filled in. Do not auto-trust
# every legacy datasource. This does not alter the platform/control DB client.
MYSQL_DATASOURCE_ALLOWED_ENDPOINTS=[]
# Format examples only: ["192.0.2.10:3306", "[2001:db8::10]:3306"]
# For DNS names such as host.docker.internal, permit every resolved numeric
# destination explicitly. Connections pin that approved IP after DNS validation.

# Per-user and application-wide probe budgets, shared atomically through Redis.
MYSQL_DATASOURCE_PROBE_USER_LIMIT=5
MYSQL_DATASOURCE_PROBE_GLOBAL_LIMIT=30
# Existing production AUTH_SESSION_BACKEND=redis and REDIS_URL are reused.
# Redis failure denies probes; never switch production to memory as a workaround.

# Deployment sequence:
# 1. UC owner disables yudao.security.mock-enable in the EFFECTIVE production
#    profile/config center. Changing mock-secret alone is insufficient.
# 2. Revoke compromised UC access/refresh tokens and application sessions using
#    the supported revocation procedures; do not FLUSHALL a shared Redis.
# 3. Review existing datasource IDs with script/migrate_config_ownership.py and
#    register business ownership or explicit public use. Missing ownership rows
#    are admin-only; historical owner text is not a tenant authorization grant.
# 4. Approve exact endpoint allowlist; inject it into API AND workers, then roll
#    out the application patch. Empty policy intentionally blocks source egress.
# 5. Rotate affected DB accounts to dedicated least-privilege accounts, restrict
#    ingress to application sources, and restrict container egress to approved
#    database destinations. Preserve DNS/UC/Redis dependencies required by app.
# 6. Correlate datasource list/detail/metadata/test accesses with UC authorize /
#    token / revocation logs and the incident time window before log retention
#    expires. Only safe IDs and probe outcomes are emitted by the new audit log.
# 7. Verify 401 anonymous, 403 ordinary/cross-business/unreviewed access,
#    sanitized shared selectors, configured-database-only developer metadata,
#    target denial before TCP, generic connection errors, and 429 probe budgets.
# No production configuration or credentials are changed by this example file.
